From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:07:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [voicecall] Forget a provider's calls when the provider goes
 away.

removeProvider() dropped the provider but kept its calls. Providers
delete their handlers themselves, without telling the manager once it no
longer listens: the ofono factory deletes the provider and its calls
when a modem goes away mid-call (ofono or the RIL restarting), and the
telepathy provider removes itself when its account goes offline. The
manager, the active call and the MCE plugin were then left with dangling
handler pointers. Reading the activeVoiceCall D-Bus property crashed,
and no later call ever became active, since the stale pointer kept the
slot taken. A telepathy account coming back announced its surviving
calls a second time, so plugins counted them twice and the D-Bus service
adapted them twice, sending every call signal twice.

Remove a provider's calls along with it, ignore calls that are already
registered, and adapt each handler for D-Bus once. Hold the active call
in a QPointer, and the MCE plugin's handlers as well.

The active call was also only ever the first call added, and none after
it ended, even with another call still up: DTMF went to a held call
after answering a waiting one, and to nothing after the first of two
calls ended. Recompute it whenever calls come, go or change state:
the connected call, else one being set up, else one ringing, else a held
one, keeping the current choice on a tie. Re-register /calls/active when
it moves from one call to another, as registerObject() refuses a path
that is still taken.

MCE also kept reporting an emergency call after it had ended; only
count calls that are still up.

Add a unit test of the manager's call bookkeeping against a fake
provider.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
